# E §4.1 (tally 2.1.7, the builder's SR-B4, pick P40): movements sort by (day, stratum, move id, keys, ...), "each term
# compared as its own type, never as text". Two decisions on one day, of moves feed and feed2 that read pocket and
# change konto: feed's entry comes first, so a projection's counted lines list it first. refcore 2.1.7 joined the move
# id and the instance as one text, `feed2|000000` before `feed|000000` (`2` below `|`); T's G5 fixtures met it once
# R5 let their runs go on (2.1.6 refused them at load).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-02-15
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-03-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index month = month 2026-01..2026-03
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place pocket: cash PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input small: money PLN
input big: money PLN
input dom: int

move feed[m in month]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  reads pocket
  leg cash from konto to shop amount if bal(pocket) > big then amt else small

move feed2[m in month]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  reads pocket
  leg cash from konto to world amount if bal(pocket) > big then amt else small

ask p: explain bal(konto, 2026-02-15) from 2026-02-01

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 5.00 PLN
  small = 1.00 PLN
  big = 10.00 PLN
  dom = 15
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[pocket] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
p: 80.00 PLN
  projection of konto (PLN) from 2026-02-01 to the end of 2026-02-15
  holder: ask p (an ask line leaves out nothing, L §5.14.1)
  clauses: windows none, random none, without uncertain
  start: 90.00 PLN at the start of 2026-02-01
  counted:
    2026-02-15:
      feed[2026-02].cash (plan): -5.00 PLN
      feed2[2026-02].cash (plan): -5.00 PLN
  left out: none
  unfulfilled: feed2[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: feed[2026-01]
  cut 2026-02-15
